derivations.claim:
*Parameter derivatives.* If $
u\in O_{h/2}$, every coordinate disc of radius $h/2$ about $
u$ lies in $O_h$: this follows directly from the triangle inequality for distance to the label set. Cauchy's estimate [F1], applied to each component of $WX_F$ on the same phase domain, therefore gives $|W\partial_{
u_j}X_F|\le CE/h$. The derivative $b_t=\partial_{
u_j}\Phi_t$ solves $b_t'=DX_F(\Phi_t)b_t+\partial_{
u_j}X_F(\Phi_t)$, $b_0=0$, by [F4]. Multiplying by $W$ and using the bounds already proved, Gronwall gives $|Wb_t|\le (CE/h)e^{L}$ for $t\le1$, which is the required estimate after increasing $C$.

